   "html": "<p>Two solids are mathematically similar. Their surface areas are 45 cm<sup>2</sup> and 80 cm<sup>2</sup>. The volume of the smaller solid is 27 cm<sup>3</sup>. Work out the volume of the larger solid.</p>",
   "answer": "<p>64 cm<sup>3</sup>. The area ratio 45:80 is 9:16, so the length ratio is 3:4 and the volume ratio is 27:64.</p>",
   "answerType": "calculation",
   "needsPrint": false,
   "examinerNote": "",
